camerabin: Nokia's camera stack on the N9, viewfinder without a copy

With GStreamer 0.10, when the phone has Nokia's subdevsrc2, the camera source is camsrcbin with
subdevsrc2 as its video source (as the stock camera's libqcamera): subdevsrc as the camera
source failed to reach READY. The cameras are listed through subdevsrc2 ("primary",
"secondary", its camera-device property; camsrcbin would list the ISP's V4L2 nodes) by the
plugin, the service's device control and its info control, so they agree. subdevsrc2 offers
YUY2 but sends UYVY: UYVY is asked for unless the app sets a format. The V4L2 parameter query
is skipped for those camera names (no V4L2 node; subdevsrc2 has GstPhotography).

The viewfinder uses gltexturesink (0002), but the camera must start with it: switched in while
starting, Nokia's source hung in the reload. So the camera's renderer is ready only once
VideoOutput has its OpenGL context (the player's isn't gated: resuming after a pause stalled),
and the renderer reacts to that context later, from the event loop (VideoOutput sets it
holding its frame mutex, which a reload's surface stop takes).

